'x_mo-definition'('x_TGMA--0000891',"&quot;In many insects, the transverse suture dividing the postmentum into a distal part, the mentum, and a proximal part, the submentum; often weak or absent; probably not homologous among all insects said to have it. In mosquito larvae, a transverse membranous area just distal to the labiogula, often hidden from below by the projecting anterior part of the labiogula; in anopheline larvae, the distal edge is limited by the well-sclerotized base of the ventromentum.&quot; [ISBN:0-937548-00-6]") :- x_cid(a65b125ad301fd).
